# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Conventional Commits (subject), 50/72 wrapping, body explains "why".
# Reference: https://www.conventionalcommits.org/
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# <type>(<optional scope>): <subject in imperative mood, ≤ 50 chars>
#
# <body — wrap at 72 chars; explain WHAT and WHY, not HOW>
#
# <footer — "BREAKING CHANGE: …" / "Refs: #123" / "Co-authored-by: …">
#
# ─── Types ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   feat:     a new feature for the user
#   fix:      a bug fix for the user
#   docs:     documentation only
#   style:    formatting, no code change
#   refactor: code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf:     performance improvement
#   test:     adding or fixing tests
#   build:    build system, CI, packaging
#   ci:       CI configuration
#   chore:    tooling, deps, non-user-facing
#   revert:   revert a previous commit
#   security: security fix
#   i18n:     translation
# ─── Scopes (use the subsystem) ──────────────────────────────────────
#   workbench · agentd · fnix-local · mcp · desktop-tauri
#   protocol · sdk · docs · ci · security · deps · release
# ─── Examples ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   feat(workbench): add diff preview accept-all shortcut
#   fix(agentd): correct retry on transient 502 from upstream LLM
#   docs: clarify BYOK keychain storage on Windows
#   perf(agentd): cache Markdown memory index (1.4s → 90ms)
#   BREAKING CHANGE: rename /v1/work to /v1/sessions/{id}/messages
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
